lus 2-ckt header on NFC&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;RED / BLACK twisted pair, 28 AWG, 102 mm&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;Molex drawing&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;PSU1 RSP-500-24&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;TB1 / TB2 / CN100&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;screw terminals / HRS DF11-04DP-2DS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;ring or fork lugs / CN100 unused&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;TB1 1 AC/L · 2 AC/N · 3 FG · TB2 1–3 −V · 4–6 +V · CN100 1 −S · 2 +S · 3 RC− · 4 RC+&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;Mean Well spec&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;J1 FN9264-6-06&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;IEC C14 inlet, fast-on terminals&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;insulated fast-on receptacles (size per datasheet)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;L · N · PE (load side)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;Schaffner/TE listing&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;MAINCTRL MYD-YF13X&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;DC / CAN / RS485 / ETH&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;native MYIR connectors&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;TBC from MYIR hardware manual&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;12 V / 2 A jack · CAN · RS485 · 2 × GbE RJ45&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;MYIR product page&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;IOCTRL ESP32-S3-ETH-8DI-8RO&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;terminals&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;screw terminals&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;bootlace ferrules&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;7–36 V · RS485 A / B / GND · RO1–8 NO / COM / NC · DI1–8 + common&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;Waveshare wiki / product page&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;J2 1422N13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;RJ45 F/F shielded coupler&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;Cat5e / Cat6 patch cords&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;1:1 pass-through&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #BDBDBD;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top;background:#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;R27 register (S05)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#212121;fontFamily=Helvetica;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="L0c"><mxGeometry x="40" y="100" width="2900" height="600" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t3rules" value="&lt;b&gt;Harness build rules used in this drawing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:4px 0 0 0;padding-left:18px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;One cable ID per physical cable (W01…W39); label both ends with W-ID and destination (e.g. W24-07 → LANECTRL-07 J8).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Project cable convention: 4-core 22 AWG red / black / yellow / green where electrically suitable; mains and higher-current pairs use rated exceptions sized per fuse / load (gauges not yet specified in the design files).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;CAN and RS485: twisted pair, 120 Ω only at the two physical bus ends; shield / drain is not protective earth — terminate it at one end only (decision pending).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Differential step signals (PUL±, DIR±, ENA±) as twisted pairs; motor phases as pairs A+/A− and B+/B−.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;IOCTRL screw terminals: bootlace ferrules. PSU1 barrier terminals: ring / fork lugs. Micro-Fit and VH crimps with the manufacturer tool.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Protective earth green / yellow; all exposed metal bonded to the chassis PE stud (W37).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build and test one step (layer) at a time: continuity, polarity and termination resistance before power-up.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#212121;fontFamily=Helvetica;strokeColor=#CFD8DC;fillColor=#FAFBFC;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="L0c"><mxGeometry x="40" y="760" width="2900" height="190" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
